{:ev/id "demo-042" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802520000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-select-0" {:concept-id "select" :kind :explanation :level :novice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Read a query starting with FROM: first where the data comes from, then what to take. SELECT name, city FROM customers — two columns from the customers table." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p12" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-043" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802580000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-select-1" {:concept-id "select" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Task: a list of email addresses of customers from Moscow. Solution: SELECT email FROM customers WHERE city = 'Moscow'. Beginner's mistake: SELECT * and filtering in Excel afterward." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p14" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-044" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802640000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-where-2" {:concept-id "where" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "WHERE is a sieve over rows. The condition is evaluated for every row; a row passes if the condition is true. NULL in the condition — the row doesn't pass." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p21" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-045" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802700000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-where-3" {:concept-id "where" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Orders from March over 1000: WHERE order_date BETWEEN '2025-03-01' AND '2025-03-31' AND amount > 1000. No parentheses needed — it's just AND." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p23" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-046" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802760000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-operators-4" {:concept-id "operators" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "AND binds tighter than OR: a OR b AND c reads as a OR (b AND c). Always add parentheses when OR is involved." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p18" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-047" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802820000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-order-by-5" {:concept-id "order-by" :kind :explanation :level :novice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "ORDER BY amount DESC, created_at — the priciest first, and for equal amounts, the earlier ones. Sorting is the last step before LIMIT." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p30" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-048" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802880000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-null-6" {:concept-id "null" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "WHERE discount = NULL never returns anything, ever. Correct form: WHERE discount IS NULL. COUNT(discount) doesn't count the empty ones." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p26" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-049" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756802940000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-agg-7" {:concept-id "agg" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "COUNT(*) — how many rows. SUM(amount) — the total. AVG(amount) — the average over non-NULL values. Without GROUP BY, an aggregate collapses the whole table into one row." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p34" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-050" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803000000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-group-by-8" {:concept-id "group-by" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "GROUP BY city sorts orders into buckets by city; SELECT city, SUM(amount) then gives one row per city. A column that's neither aggregated nor in GROUP BY is an error." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p36" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-051" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803060000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-group-by-9" {:concept-id "group-by" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Revenue by month: SELECT date_trunc('month', order_date) AS m, SUM(amount) FROM orders GROUP BY m ORDER BY m." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p38" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-052" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803120000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-group-by-10" {:concept-id "group-by" :kind :diagram :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Diagram: 9 order rows → three buckets (Moscow, Kazan, Perm) → three rows with totals. Arrows show which bucket each row landed in." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p37" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-053" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803180000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-having-11" {:concept-id "having" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "HAVING COUNT(*) > 10 keeps only the buckets with more than ten orders. The same condition in WHERE is a syntax error: the rows haven't been grouped yet." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p40" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-054" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803240000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-having-12" {:concept-id "having" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Cities with revenue over a million in 2025: WHERE on the date (rows), GROUP BY city, HAVING SUM(amount) > 1000000 (groups)." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p41" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-055" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803300000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-keys-13" {:concept-id "keys" :kind :explanation :level :novice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "orders.customer_id → customers.id: an order carries its customer's id. Tables get joined on exactly this kind of pair. A key isn't \"an important column\" — it's a promise of uniqueness." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p46" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-056" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803360000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-join-14" {:concept-id "join" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "FROM orders JOIN customers ON orders.customer_id = customers.id — each order gets its customer attached. Orders without a customer and customers without orders drop out." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p48" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-057" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803420000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-join-15" {:concept-id "join" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Customer name next to the order amount: SELECT c.name, o.amount FROM orders o JOIN customers c ON o.customer_id = c.id." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p50" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-058" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803480000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-join-16" {:concept-id "join" :kind :diagram :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Two tables as two columns of cards, lines between matching ids; the result is only the joined pairs." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p49" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-059" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803540000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-left-join-17" {:concept-id "left-join" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Customers with no orders: LEFT JOIN orders … WHERE orders.id IS NULL. Write WHERE orders.amount > 0 instead, and the empty rows get filtered out — LEFT quietly becomes INNER." :grounded-in "src-pg-docs" :anchor "p52" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-060" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803600000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-subquery-18" {:concept-id "subquery" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "WHERE customer_id IN (SELECT id FROM customers WHERE city = 'Kazan') — the inner query hands back a list, and the outer query filters against it." :grounded-in "src-sql-book" :anchor "p56" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-061" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803660000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-cte-19" {:concept-id "cte" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "WITH monthly AS (…) SELECT … FROM monthly — first you name the intermediate result, then use it like a table. A long query stops being a matryoshka doll." :grounded-in "src-pg-docs" :anchor "p60" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-062" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803720000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-window-20" {:concept-id "window" :kind :explanation :level :professional :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "SUM(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY city ORDER BY order_date) — a running total per city, while every order row stays right where it was." :grounded-in "src-pg-docs" :anchor "p66" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "demo-063" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1756803780000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "i-select-1" {:primary-concept-id "select" :level :apprentice :kind :single-choice :locale "en" :spec {:stem "Which query returns only customer names?" :options ["SELECT * FROM customers" "SELECT name FROM customers" "SELECT customers FROM name"] :key 1} :is :item}]]}
